  "id": "motor-equivalence",
  "term": "motor equivalence",
  "definition": "Motor equivalence is the principle that the same action goal can be achieved by using different body parts as the movement’s effective end point. In the source, this is illustrated by reaching or avoidance behavior that can be directed through arbitrary selected body parts.",
